zip_area_code_map.parquet

Population and geography: U.S. Census Bureau, 2023 ACS five-year table B01003,
2023 national ZCTA Gazetteer, and 2023 TIGER/Line state shapefiles.
U.S. government works are public domain in the United States. TIGER/Line
metadata permits use in products/publications with Census source acknowledgment.
TIGER/Line is a registered trademark of the U.S. Census Bureau. This product is
not endorsed or certified by the Census Bureau. Boundaries are statistical
representations, not legal land descriptions.
https://www2.census.gov/geo/pdfs/maps-data/data/tiger/tgrshp2023/TGRSHP2023_TechDoc.pdf

Locality, postal-code, and dialing-code statements: Wikidata contributors,
structured-data snapshots retrieved 2026-11-06, CC0 1.0 Universal.
CC0 permits copying, modification, and redistribution, including commercially,
without attribution or share-alike requirements.
https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Wikidata:Licensing
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

Transformation: normalize locality statements, remove curated exclusions,
prefer nearby same-state literal postal-code associations, and otherwise use
the nearest same-state locality. Population weights come directly from Census.
This is an approximation for synthetic data, not exact telephone boundaries.

NANPA's 2026-11-06 NPA report was consulted only as a screening reference.
No explicit open-data license was established for that report. It is not
redistributed and is not required to rebuild from the pinned snapshots.

Source URLs, hashes, queries, exclusions, methodology, and rebuild instructions:
https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/DataDesigner/tree/main/scripts/person_data
